# SS-11 - Verified Windows packaging and acceptance
Workstream ID: SS-11
GitHub issue: https://github.com/Zanark/StonksSniper/issues/11
Status: IN_PROGRESS
Milestone: M4
Dependencies: SS-05, SS-07, SS-10

## Purpose
Deliver a repeatable native Windows package with honest runtime and acceptance evidence.

## Tasks
- [x] Add Windows/Linux regression CI and an explicit live-provider test mode.
- [x] Build and publish the separately authorized v0.2.0 executable prototype.
- [ ] Lock release dependencies and review redistribution/license notices.
- [ ] Produce isolated installer/portable candidate and test a clean Windows profile.
- [ ] Verify startup, Qt plugins, networking, Unicode paths, exports and recovery.
- [ ] Test keyboard access, scaling, large histories and worker shutdown behaviour.
- [ ] Record human acceptance and separately authorized release/publication.

## Acceptance criteria
- Source launch, packaged launch, visual inspection and user acceptance remain distinct.
- No user instance is restarted or overwritten during development qualification.

## Completion evidence
- Published the separate v0.2.0 standalone prototype; broader M4 acceptance is open.
  Source-native Windows diagnostics fetched actual HDFCBANK history, exercised
  27 rules and exported the exact experiment without showing/controlling a user
  window. The full local suite including opt-in live checks passed 211 tests.
  An isolated pinned build environment leaves the existing .venv untouched.
  Qt Charts requires GPLv3/commercial terms: this open prototype adopts GPLv3,
  includes licenses and documents equivalent-access source/rebuild locations.
- A local standalone candidate built, but this machine's Application Control
  blocked its extracted Python DLL before initialization. No policy workaround
  was attempted; hosted Windows packaged-runtime verification passed separately.
  Local frozen/Unicode runtime qualification is not claimed.
- Release: https://github.com/Zanark/StonksSniper/releases/tag/v0.2.0
  Exact clean source: 9284b00bc9647f65c76bf81d96e2d79cef1cdbb6.
  Windows/Linux live CI:
  https://github.com/Zanark/StonksSniper/actions/runs/43120473704
  Both platforms passed; the actual Windows EXE fetched 493 HDFCBANK bars,
  simulated all 27 strategies and exported the experiment. All four published
  assets were downloaded again and matched the verified CI artifacts exactly.
  Checksums, all 24 build inputs and the 330-entry notices archive were checked.
  The EXE remains unsigned; clean-profile/DPI/human acceptance are not implied.
- The separately authorized
  v0.1.0 prototype Python wheel was built and launched from a separate installation
  target with existing dependencies; its logo and theme notice were verified.
  This is not a standalone executable, clean-machine dependency test, installer
  qualification or recorded human acceptance.

## Completion log
- 2026-11-12: Published and downloaded/hash-verified v0.2.0 after exact-source
  Windows/Linux live CI passed. Tag remains at the built source, not a later
  documentation commit. Keep this workstream open for its broader acceptance.
- 2026-11-12: User authorized executable creation, a new prototype release, an
  HDFCBANK fetch fix and GitHub Actions tests. Preserve frozen v0.1.0.
  Added read-only Windows/Linux CI with pinned Actions, an explicit live mode
  and actual frozen-runtime checks. Local source/live suite passed 211 tests.
- 2026-11-11: Registered packaging and acceptance gates.
- 2026-11-11: User authorized first-prototype commit, push and GitHub release.
  Built/smoke-tested the Python wheel without restarting any existing user app.
  Dedicated M4 qualification and clean-profile acceptance remain planned.
